== 1.8 Chapter 1 Practice Drill — 30 Questions

30 questions graded in the order the CBT engine is likely to meet them. Allow 33 minutes; the key and a full solution for every question follow.

#mcq(1, [Which of the following is *not* a characteristic of living things?],
  [Excretion],
  [Respiration],
  [Crystallisation],
  [Irritability]
)

#mcq(2, [The seven characteristics of living things are remembered by the mnemonic],
  [MRS CERN],
  [MRS GREN],
  [DNA-RNA],
  [ATP-ADP]
)

#mcq(3, [A crystal left in a saturated solution becomes larger. This is not biological growth because],
  [it takes too long],
  [it needs light],
  [it stops in the dark],
  [it has no cells and does not assimilate food]
)

#mcq(4, [The removal of undigested food material from the alimentary canal is called],
  [digestion],
  [secretion],
  [egestion],
  [excretion]
)

#mcq(5, [Urea is an excretory product because it is],
  [produced by the kidneys from water],
  [formed inside the body by the breakdown of amino acids],
  [undigested food],
  [secreted by the liver into the gut]
)

#mcq(6, [The correct order of the taxonomic ranks, from largest to smallest, is],
  [Kingdom, class, phylum, family, order, genus, species],
  [Species, genus, family, order, class, phylum, kingdom],
  [Phylum, kingdom, order, class, family, species, genus],
  [Kingdom, phylum, class, order, family, genus, species]
)

#mcq(7, [A group of organisms that can interbreed to produce fertile offspring is a],
  [genus],
  [family],
  [species],
  [population]
)

#mcq(8, [Organisms with no true nucleus belong to the kingdom],
  [Protista],
  [Fungi],
  [Monera],
  [Plantae]
)

#mcq(9, [Which kingdom contains organisms with a cell wall made of chitin?],
  [Fungi],
  [Animalia],
  [Protista],
  [Monera]
)

#mcq(10, [An organism is single-celled, has a nucleus, moves with cilia and has no cell wall. Its kingdom is],
  [Plantae],
  [Monera],
  [Fungi],
  [Protista]
)

#mcq(11, [Which of these is a characteristic feature of the kingdom Plantae?],
  [Cellulose cell walls and chlorophyll],
  [Heterotrophic nutrition by ingestion],
  [Chitin cell walls],
  [No true nucleus]
)

#mcq(12, [Viruses are not classified in any of the five kingdoms because],
  [they have no cellular organisation and no independent metabolism],
  [they are too small to see],
  [they cause disease],
  [they contain DNA]
)

#mcq(13, [A virus consists essentially of],
  [a cell wall and a cell membrane],
  [a nucleus and cytoplasm],
  [a nucleic acid core and a protein coat],
  [chloroplasts and mitochondria]
)

#mcq(14, [Which of the following is a viral disease of plants?],
  [Rust of maize],
  [Blight of tomato],
  [Cassava mosaic disease],
  [Root rot]
)

#mcq(15, [The scientific name of man is written correctly as],
  [*Homo sapiens*],
  [*HOMO SAPIENS*],
  [*homo sapiens*],
  [*Homo Sapiens*]
)

#mcq(16, [The genus of the lion is],
  [*leo*],
  [*Animalia*],
  [*Felis*],
  [*Panthera*]
)

#mcq(17, [Two organisms have the names *Panthera leo* and *Panthera tigris*. They belong to the same],
  [family only],
  [kingdom only],
  [genus],
  [species]
)

#mcq(18, [Which statement about fungi is correct?],
  [They have chitin walls and feed saprophytically or parasitically],
  [They are prokaryotic],
  [They store starch],
  [They photosynthesise]
)

#mcq(19, [Bacteria are placed in a separate kingdom from blue-green algae in modern classification, but both are],
  [prokaryotic],
  [photosynthetic animals],
  [multicellular],
  [eukaryotic]
)

#mcq(20, [A characteristic shared by all living organisms is],
  [the ability to reproduce],
  [the ability to photosynthesise],
  [the possession of a cell wall],
  [the ability to move from place to place]
)

#mcq(21, [A dead leaf and a stone are both non-living in everyday speech. Biologically],
  [neither can be classified],
  [the leaf was once living, the stone never was],
  [both were once living],
  [both are non-living]
)

#mcq(22, [The unit below the kingdom in the plant taxonomic hierarchy is called a],
  [class],
  [order],
  [division],
  [family]
)

#mcq(23, [Which of the following would be classified in the kingdom Protista?],
  [*Amoeba*],
  [Maize],
  [*Escherichia coli*],
  [*Rhizopus*]
)

#mcq(24, [The binomial system of nomenclature was introduced by],
  [Gregor Mendel],
  [Carl Linnaeus],
  [Charles Darwin],
  [Louis Pasteur]
)

#mcq(25, [Antibiotics do not cure viral diseases because],
  [viruses live in the blood],
  [antibiotics are destroyed by mucus],
  [viruses are too large],
  [viruses have no metabolism or cell structure for the antibiotic to attack]
)

#mcq(26, [Which characteristic is shown by a plant bending towards light?],
  [Sensitivity],
  [Respiration],
  [Nutrition],
  [Excretion]
)

#mcq(27, [Which of these is the correct sequence of increasing similarity?],
  [Order → class → genus → family],
  [Class → order → family → genus],
  [Genus → family → order → class],
  [Family → class → order → genus]
)

#mcq(28, [Organisms that are multicellular, have no cell wall and feed by ingestion belong to],
  [Protista],
  [Animalia],
  [Fungi],
  [Plantae]
)

#mcq(29, [The part of a virus that enters the host cell is],
  [the whole virus],
  [the nucleic acid],
  [the protein coat only],
  [the tail fibres]
)

#mcq(30, [A species is best defined as a group of organisms that],
  [live in the same habitat],
  [belong to the same genus],
  [can interbreed to produce fertile offspring],
  [look alike]
)

