=== Complete Solutions

#sol-item(1, "C", dense: true)[
  Crystallisation is a physical process by which a dissolved solid comes out of solution. It requires no cells and no metabolism, so it is not a characteristic of life.
]

#sol-item(2, "B", dense: true)[
  Movement, Respiration, Sensitivity, Growth, Reproduction, Excretion, Nutrition — MRS GREN.
]

#sol-item(3, "D", dense: true)[
  Biological growth is a permanent increase in size or mass produced by cell division and cell enlargement; a crystal merely gains deposited material.
]

#sol-item(4, "C", dense: true)[
  Egestion removes material that was never absorbed and so was never part of metabolism; excretion removes metabolic waste made inside the cells.
]

#sol-item(5, "B", dense: true)[
  Urea is made inside the body from the deamination of excess amino acids, so removing it is excretion.
]

#sol-item(6, "D", dense: true)[
  Kingdom → Phylum → Class → Order → Family → Genus → Species. A useful check: the species is the smallest and must come last.
]

#sol-item(7, "C", dense: true)[
  That is the definition of a species. A horse and a donkey produce a sterile mule, so they remain two species.
]

#sol-item(8, "C", dense: true)[
  Monera is the only kingdom of prokaryotes: no true nucleus and no membrane-bound organelles.
]

#sol-item(9, "A", dense: true)[
  Fungal walls are chitin; plant walls are cellulose and bacterial walls peptidoglycan.
]

#sol-item(10, "D", dense: true)[
  Eukaryotic, single-celled, motile and wall-less — the animal-like protists, such as Paramecium.
]

#sol-item(11, "A", dense: true)[
  Plants are multicellular, have cellulose walls, contain chlorophyll and photosynthesise.
]

#sol-item(12, "A", dense: true)[
  A virus is not a cell: no cytoplasm, no nucleus, no organelles, and no metabolism of its own. It is an obligate intracellular parasite.
]

#sol-item(13, "C", dense: true)[
  Nucleic acid (DNA or RNA) inside a protein capsid — nothing else is essential.
]

#sol-item(14, "C", dense: true)[
  Cassava mosaic, tobacco mosaic and cocoa swollen shoot are all viral; the others are fungal or bacterial.
]

#sol-item(15, "A", dense: true)[
  Genus capitalised, species in small letters, both italic. Underlined when handwritten.
]

#sol-item(16, "D", dense: true)[
  The first word of a binomial name is the genus: *Panthera leo*.
]

#sol-item(17, "C", dense: true)[
  They share the first word, so they share the genus; they differ in the species, so they are different species.
]

#sol-item(18, "A", dense: true)[
  Fungi are eukaryotic heterotrophs with chitin walls; they digest food outside the body and absorb it.
]

#sol-item(19, "A", dense: true)[
  Both are prokaryotes; cyanobacteria are photosynthetic bacteria and are classified in Monera.
]

#sol-item(20, "A", dense: true)[
  Reproduction is universal; photosynthesis, locomotion and cell walls are not.
]

#sol-item(21, "B", dense: true)[
  A dead thing once showed the characteristics of life; a non-living thing never did.
]

#sol-item(22, "C", dense: true)[
  Botanists use *division* where zoologists use *phylum*.
]

#sol-item(23, "A", dense: true)[
  *Amoeba* is a single-celled eukaryote, so it belongs to Protista; *Rhizopus* is a fungus, maize a plant and *E. coli* a bacterium.
]

#sol-item(24, "B", dense: true)[
  Linnaeus introduced the two-word naming system in the eighteenth century.
]

#sol-item(25, "D", dense: true)[
  Antibiotics act on bacterial structures and processes; a virus has neither, so there is nothing for the drug to target.
]

#sol-item(26, "A", dense: true)[
  It is a response to a stimulus — phototropism — and falls under sensitivity; it is a growth movement, not locomotion.
]

#sol-item(27, "B", dense: true)[
  Working down the hierarchy, each rank contains organisms that are more alike: class, then order, then family, then genus.
]

#sol-item(28, "B", dense: true)[
  No cell wall plus ingestion is the animal plan; fungi have walls and absorb, plants have walls and photosynthesise.
]

#sol-item(29, "B", dense: true)[
  Only the nucleic acid enters; the capsid usually remains outside. That is why a virus cannot be said to 'eat' or 'respire'.
]

#sol-item(30, "C", dense: true)[
  Appearance can mislead; breeding and fertile offspring are the test.
]

